Critical bug hit + fix
- Initial implementation segfaulted on `test/match_recursive_arg` (AOT only).
- ASan trace showed deep recursive cycle:
  - `aot_force_whnf_local -> wnf -> aot_try_call -> F_mat_self -> ...`
  - stack overflow due forcing path re-entering compiled calls recursively.
- Root cause:
  - strict local forcing called `wnf`, and `wnf` REF path used `aot_try_call` (compiled re-entry), which is not depth-guarded.
- Fix landed:
  - Added thread-local gate `AOT_TRY_CALL_ENABLED` (default on).
  - `aot_try_call` returns 0 when gate is off.
  - `aot_force_whnf_local` now temporarily disables `aot_try_call` around `wnf(term)`, forcing REF handling through interpreter ALO expansion instead of recursive compiled re-entry.
  - This preserves correctness and eliminates the stack-overflow regression.

